1
00:00:09,536 --> 00:00:17,536
Warden — an SRE agent for long-running compute jobs on Google Cloud.
RUNNING is not the same as training correctly; DONE is not the same as intact.

2
00:00:24,539 --> 00:00:32,539
Every incident carries evidence, cost and an audit trail — no LLM ever holds the button.

3
00:00:41,478 --> 00:00:55,478
Scene 1 — a real Spot preemption today: TERMINATED without RUN_FIN
→ policy level L2 → START → resumed from the last phase. Loss: 348 seconds.

4
00:01:02,559 --> 00:01:14,559
Scene 2 — finished is not intact: the verifier OPENS pred.csv
(1030 rows, sha256 match) before the job becomes COMPLETE.

5
00:01:21,655 --> 00:01:31,655
Scene 3 — an idle machine after its job completed: orphan detected,
STOP proposed with the projected cost, a human is asked.

6
00:01:39,325 --> 00:01:49,325
Ledger, projection, ETTR (effective training time ratio) and the budget kill-switch.

7
00:01:56,238 --> 00:02:04,238
Graduated autonomy per action type.
Delete does not exist as an action — not even with approval.

8
00:02:11,142 --> 00:02:19,142
Intent before, result after: requested-vs-actual for every action.

9
00:02:26,035 --> 00:02:34,035
Success leaves a trace: Warden's own heartbeat is watched by an external dead-man service.
